<title>UK: Euromarket turnover rose in week to 31 July  -ISMA.</title>
<headline>Euromarket turnover rose in week to 31 July  -ISMA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turnover in the Eurobond and related markets rose to $1.123 trillion in the week to July 31 from $1.073 trillion in the previous week, International Securities Market Association figures show (in billions of dollars).</p>
<p>					    LATEST WEEK	PREVIOUS WEEK</p>
<p> PRIMARY MARKET:			   58.48		     48.47</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	  28.67		     27.84</p>
<p> SECONDARY MARKET:		     1064.61		   1025.50</p>
<p> OF WHICH U.S. DOLLAR ISSUES:	 796.80		    748.37</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH EUROCLEAR	    813.15		    771.18</p>
<p> CLEARED THROUGH CEDEL		  309.94		    302.15</p>
<p>--London newsroom,  +44 171 542 7658</p>
